  "prefLabel": "Env-A 4602.33 Compliance account",
  "priorExpiration": "2009-03-30",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 4602.33 “Compliance account” means a CO2 allowance tracking system account, established by the regional organization for a CO2 budget source under Env-A 4607, in which the CO2 allowance allocations for the source are initially recorded, and in which are held CO2 allowances available for use by the source for a control period and each interim control period for the purpose of meeting the requirements of Env-A 4605.\n\nSource. #9283, INTERIM, eff 10-1-08, EXPIRED: 3-30-09\n\nNew. #9444, eff 4-3-09; ss by #10468, eff 1-1-14 (from Env-A 4602.32); ss by #12967, eff 1-1-20 (from Env-A 4602.34)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a4600.html"
